<Prose title="How We Choose" eyebrow="Editorial standards" description="The criteria Electroys uses to pick STEM kits and gifts, and how we keep recommendations honest and current.">
  <p class="lead">Every product on Electroys is chosen by hand. Here is exactly what we look for, and what we don’t do.</p>
  <h2>What earns a spot</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>It teaches something real.</strong> Coding logic, circuits, mechanics, chemistry, spatial reasoning, strategy. We describe the specific skills on every product page.</li>
    <li><strong>Kids want to play with it twice.</strong> Replay value matters more than a flashy box.</li>
    <li><strong>A trusted maker.</strong> We favor established brands with clear age guidance, safety information and support, and we avoid anonymous listings and knock-offs.</li>
    <li><strong>It’s honest about what it needs.</strong> If a kit needs a tablet, batteries, a computer or a lot of adult help, we say so up front.</li>
    <li><strong>It fits its age band.</strong> We follow the manufacturer’s age guidance and place products where the challenge is right, not just where it’s allowed.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>How we research</h2>
  <p>We review manufacturer documentation, product listings, instructions and published specifications, and we cross-check details like age ranges and battery requirements across sources. Where sources disagree, we use the more conservative guidance and mention it. We don’t claim hands-on testing unless we’ve actually done it.</p>
  <h2>Keeping it current</h2>
  <p>Our product links are checked automatically every week, and anything that looks discontinued or unavailable is flagged for review, then removed or replaced. Each product page shows when its listing was last verified.</p>
  <h2>What we don’t do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don’t accept payment for placement or for positive coverage.</li>
    <li>We don’t publish made-up prices, ratings or “bestseller” claims. Prices are shown as typical ranges; the retailer sets the actual price.</li>
    <li>We don’t let commissions decide our picks. Many of our favorites are inexpensive.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If you spot an error, an outdated listing or a safety concern, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. We fix confirmed problems promptly.</p>
</Prose>
